../items/lem-positive-half-plane-maps-have-controlled-boundary-and-plumbing-limits.md:48:1.2 Here is the required quantitative edge bound. Scale the large half-disk to the unit one. Oddly reflect a harmonic $u$ with zero diameter values across the diameter. Its weak first derivatives match across the edge, since its zero tangential derivative and reflected normal derivative agree; the distributional Laplacian has no line atom. Local disk convolution and the circle mean identity make that weak harmonic extension smooth. On a slightly smaller disk its boundary values are $u(e^{it})$ on the upper semicircle and their negatives on the lower. A harmonic conjugate on a disk is obtained by integrating the closed form $u_y\,dx-u_x\,dy$ from its center; triangle Green integration makes the integral path independent. The ordinary Poisson identity then follows directly from the circle Cauchy formula for this conjugate, or by expanding the kernel $\operatorname{Re}((e^{it}+z)/(e^{it}-z))$ in its convergent geometric series and comparing its harmonic boundary values by the maximum principle. The maximum principle itself follows from the interior circle mean identity. Subtracting the two semicircles, the kernel for $z$ in the upper disk is $$\frac1{2\pi}\bigl(P(z,e^{it})-P(z,e^{-it})\bigr)=\frac{2(1-|z|^2)\operatorname{Im}z\sin t}{\pi|e^{it}-z|^2|e^{-it}-z|^2}.$$ It is positive. For a fixed interior $z_*=i/2$, every fixed derivative in $z$ of this kernel on $|z|\le1/3$ is bounded in absolute value by $C_k$ times its value at $z_*$: all denominators are uniformly separated from zero and both numerator formulas have the factor $\sin t$. Integrating against the NONNEGATIVE upper semicircle data proves $\sup_{|z|\le1/3}|D^ku(z)|\le C_ku(z_*)$. Using a slightly smaller containing disk if necessary avoids any corner regularity issue at the two diameter endpoints. The Cauchy--Riemann identities bound derivatives of the real part of a holomorphic $p$ by those of $u$. One known interior real value and integration on the smaller connected set bound the remaining additive real constant. Smooth fixed coordinate changes give exactly the same estimates in the boundary and square-root charts specified in the Statement. [F1, given, construct, algebra]
../items/lem-bounded-punctured-slice-has-holomorphic-parameter-extension.md:55:[L3] The one-variable Cauchy integral formula recovers a holomorphic function on a disc from a circle inside it ([[thm-cauchy-integral-formula-circle]]).
