../items/thm-cauchy-integral-formula-and-cauchy-estimates-for-banach-valued-holomorphic-functions.md:80:3.1 Cauchy's integral formula. Put $J:=\oint_{C_r}h(w)\,dw=0$. Writing $\frac{F(w)}{w-z}=\frac{F(z)}{w-z}+\frac{F(w)-F(z)}{w-z}$ and using [step 2.1] and [step 1.2], $\frac1{2\pi i}\oint_{C_r}\frac{F(w)}{w-z}\,dw=\frac{F(z)}{2\pi i}\oint_{C_r}\frac{dw}{w-z}+\frac{J}{2\pi i}=F(z)$. [step 1.2, step 2.1, L2, given, algebra]
